---
// Virtual office guide 1. Legal points must be checked against gov.uk before publishing (Blueprint 04 · Check before the push).
import Guide from '../../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { address, formatPrice, virtualOffice, withCover } from '../../../data/facts';
import { guideBySlug } from '../../../data/guides';

const guide = guideBySlug('home-address-companies-house');
const [p20, p40] = virtualOffice.plans;
const dc = virtualOffice.directorsCover;

const title = "Home Address Off Companies House | Maggie O'Neill Centre";
const description =
  "Which addresses Companies House shows, how to swap your home for a business address, and what to do about older filings. A guide from Maggie O'Neill Centre.";

const answer =
  "Give Companies House a business address for two things: your company's registered office and your director's service address. New filings then show the business address, not your home. Older documents keep the address they were filed with. But you can apply to have your home address removed from some of them.";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Is my home address on Companies House?',
    a: "It is if you used it as your company's registered office. It's also there if you used it as your correspondence (service) address. That applies to a director or a person with significant control. The Companies House register is public. Anyone can search it online for free.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I stop my home address showing on Companies House?',
    a: "Yes, for new filings. Change your company's registered office and your director's service address to a business address. Companies House then shows that address from then on. Your residential address is still collected. But it isn't shown on the public register when you give a separate service address.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Will my old address disappear from Companies House?',
    a: 'Not by itself. Documents filed before the change still show the address they were filed with. Companies House lets you apply to remove your home address from some older documents. Gov.uk lists the current form and fee.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I use a PO box as my registered office?',
    a: "No. Companies House doesn't accept a PO box as a registered office. The registered office has to be an appropriate address. That means post sent to the company would reach someone acting for it, and they could acknowledge it.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Does a sole trader appear on Companies House?',
    a: "No. Sole traders don't register with Companies House. So a sole trader's home address isn't on the Companies House register. It may still be on your website, invoices and listings. A business address keeps it off those too.",
  },
  {
    q: "How much does it cost to keep my home address off Companies House with the Maggie O'Neill Centre?",
    a: `At the Maggie O'Neill Centre, a registered office address costs ${formatPrice(p20.price)} a month. Director's Cover adds a director's service address for ${formatPrice(dc.price)} a month. So both together cost ${formatPrice(withCover(p20))} a month.`,
  },
];
---
<Guide
  guide={guide}
  title={title}
  description={description}
  tagline="Keep your front door off the register."
  answer={answer}
  faqs={faqs}
  cta={{
    heading: 'Get a registered office address near Liverpool',
    text: `A real address at ${address.street}, Huyton, from ${formatPrice(p20.price)} a month. Add Director's Cover for ${formatPrice(dc.price)} a month. Then your home comes off new filings in both places.`,
    href: '/services/virtual-office/',
    label: 'Registered office address Liverpool',
  }}
>
  <h2>Why is my home address on Companies House?</h2>
  <p>
    The Companies House register is public. Anyone can search it online, for free. They can see the addresses your company has filed. Many
    directors set up their company from home. They used their home address because it was the easiest thing to put on the form.
  </p>
  <p>Your home address can appear on the register in three places:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The registered office.</strong> Your company's official address. It's shown on the register and on your company's documents.</li>
    <li><strong>Your service address as a director.</strong> The address Companies House and others use to write to you as a director.</li>
    <li><strong>Your service address as a person with significant control (PSC).</strong> If you own or control the company, you'll be listed as a PSC too.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Companies House also collects your usual residential address. It isn't shown on the public register, as long as you've given a
    separate service address. Only the month and year of your date of birth are shown to the public.
  </p>

  <h2>How do I take my home address off Companies House?</h2>
  <p>It takes two changes, and you can make both online with Companies House.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Change your registered office address.</strong> Move it to a business address you're allowed to use, such as a
      {' '}<a href="/services/virtual-office/">virtual office in Liverpool</a>. It becomes your registered office once Companies
      House registers the change. For 14 days after that, documents can still be validly delivered to the old address.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Change your service address as a director and as a PSC.</strong> Swap your home for a director's service address. Your
      residential address then stays private on the register.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="note">
    Changing only the registered office isn't enough. If your home is still your service address, it stays on the public register. You
    have to change the two separately.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens to my old filings?</h2>
  <p>
    Documents filed before the change keep the address they were filed with. That includes your incorporation documents and earlier
    confirmation statements. Changing your address doesn't rewrite them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Companies House lets you apply to remove your home address from some older documents on the register. There's a fee for each document.
    You'll need to give a service address to use instead. See the
    {' '}<a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/companies-house" rel="noopener">Companies House guidance on gov.uk</a>. It has the form, the current fee and which documents qualify. Look for removing your home address from the register.
  </p>

  <h2>What counts as a business address for Companies House?</h2>
  <p>
    Your registered office has to be an appropriate address. That means post sent to your company would reach someone acting for it,
    and they could acknowledge it. A PO box doesn't count.
  </p>
  <p>
    A virtual office is a real address in a building with staff, so it meets that test. At the Maggie O'Neill Centre, our team
    handles virtual office post ourselves. We do it at reception, {address.oneLine}.
  </p>

  <h2>Which option do I need?</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Your situation</th><th scope="col">What to change</th><th scope="col">At Maggie's</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Only your registered office is your home (your service address is already somewhere else)</td>
          <td>The registered office</td>
          <td>{p20.name}, {formatPrice(p20.price)} a month</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Your home is the registered office and your director's service address</td>
          <td>Both</td>
          <td>{p20.name} + {dc.name}, {formatPrice(withCover(p20))} a month</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Both, and you want your post scanned and meeting rooms for clients</td>
          <td>Both</td>
          <td>{p40.name} + {dc.name}, {formatPrice(withCover(p40))} a month</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>{virtualOffice.terms}</p>

  <h2>Do I need to tell anyone else?</h2>
  <p>
    Companies House doesn't pass your new address on to anyone else. Once the change is registered, update your address on:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>your website</li>
    <li>invoices and letterheads</li>
    <li>your Google Business Profile</li>
    <li>anywhere else your home address was published for the business</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="callout">
    Not sure which addresses to change? Call us and we'll talk it through. Maybe you'd like a business address on your invoices as well as your
    registered office. Every <a href="/services/virtual-office/">virtual office plan at the Maggie O'Neill Centre</a> covers both.
  </p>
</Guide>
